{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The beloved of YHWH shall dwell in safety beside Him</b> — Benjamin is called 'the beloved of YHWH.' He says: Benjamin, who is the beloved of HaShem, shall dwell in his land in safety, relying upon HaShem, and HaShem shall hover over him all the days and cause His Shekhinah to rest within his land. <b>Between His shoulders</b> — this alludes to what our Rabbis expounded concerning it (Zevaḥim 54a). \n\nAnd by way of truth, 'the beloved of YHWH' shall dwell upon Benjamin, and this shall be a guarantee for Benjamin, that they shall trust in HaShem forever, for ביה YHWH is the Rock of eternity, and He shall hover over and shield Benjamin all the day, and they shall not be ashamed in the time of distress, and between Benjamin's shoulders He shall dwell forever. From here Solomon was called Yedidyah for the sake of YHWH (II Samuel 12:25), and he built 'the beloved's dwelling-places' (יְדִידוּת מִשְׁכְּנֹתָיו), as Solomon too was called, to say that his measure was perfect in peace, and therefore it was written with a ה (in יְדִידוּת). And they said in the midrash of Rabbi Neḥunya ben HaKannah: The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, 'Since your name is like the Name of My glory, I shall give you My daughter,' as it is written (I Kings 5:26), 'And YHWH gave wisdom to Solomon,' and it does not specify — and where does it specify? Further on (I Kings 3:28), 'For they saw that the wisdom of Elohim was within him to execute justice,' etc. \n\nAnd the matter is correct that he alludes by means of these three [mentions of] dwelling/resting to the three Sanctuaries: of the First Sanctuary he says, 'shall dwell in safety beside Him,' in the manner stated (II Chronicles 7:1), 'And the glory of YHWH filled the House'; and of the Second House he said, 'hover over him all the day,' for the Shekhinah did not dwell in it, but only covered and shielded it, or hovered literally as mentioned in the chapters of the Heikhalot; and 'between His shoulders' — He shall dwell in the days of the Messiah, for 'in that day they shall call Jerusalem the throne of YHWH' (Jeremiah 3:17). And in this manner it is expounded in the Sifrei (Berakha 332)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The phrase ובנה ידידות משכנתיו is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally as 'he built the beloved's dwelling-places.' The subject is Solomon, whose name connects to shalom and whose appellation Yedidyah ('beloved of YHWH') links him to the blessing over Benjamin."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:00.611550333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}